{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And whatever the zav touches</b> etc. This verse is not in its proper place here — it belongs after ״וכי יטהר הזב מזובו״ (and when the zav is cleansed of his flow). Rather, since it had already begun with the touch-transmissions of the zav, it wrote them all in one place." "<b>And his hands he did not wash in water.</b> Rabbi Elazar ben Arakh said: from here they derived the obligation of washing hands from the Torah. And it is a euphemistic expression — it expressed immersion in the language of washing hands. So too we find: ״ארחץ בנקיון כפי״ (I wash in cleanliness my hands)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:12:25.171543732Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}